 - `budget.json` + `budget.json.lock`: the newest `rate_limits` reading across wrapped sessions, timestamped, last-writer-wins. As landed (chunk 2026-10-10-statusline-pass-through) the file is `{"v":1,"five_hour":…,"seven_day":…,"read_at":"<RFC 3339 UTC, milliseconds>"}`. A window is the word `"unknown"` or `{used_percentage, resets_at}`, and either field may be `"unknown"`. It is replaced whole through `replace_private` at 0600 under an exclusive lock on `budget.json.lock` (`viola_state::budget::write_budget`). Written only by `hook statusline`, and only when the payload holds a `rate_limits` object, so a payload without one leaves the last reading standing. Read by each wrapper's budget gate ([Budget Governor]), and by `list` for its payload's top-level `budget`. The file has one checked read, `viola_state::budget::read_budget_stamped(home) -> Option<StampedReading>` (`{reading, read_at}`; chunk 2026-10-11-the-board-viola-list), with two product paths: the gate's `read_budget(home) -> Option<BudgetReading>` (chunk 2026-10-10-budget-governor), now `read_budget_stamped(home).map(|s| s.reading)`, and `viola list`. `read_at` is `"unknown"` when the key is absent or no string. The read runs, in order: `strict::check_path` on the home, `check_path` on `budget.json`, a shared lock on `budget.json.lock`, the bytes through `take(MAX_FRAME + 1)` (over the cap is no reading), a tolerant parse that skips an unknown key, and no reading unless `v` is 1. Every failure is no reading, with no log line. It never writes `budget.json`, and an absent file under a home that passes its check creates nothing, the lock sibling included. The wrapper refusing a driver on this file, which a hook arm writes and the trusted-file list does not hold, is a boundary widening the founder ratified: his own answer, 2026-10-13, relayed verbatim by the Viola overseer, ratifies it as built — read behind the strict-modes check on the home and the file, failing open (it had landed on the operator's word, 2026-10-10, which is no ratification; superseded 2026-10-13) (security-plan §Authentication & Authorization, `~/.viola/` access control).
